So what do you do with a unicorn horn?
Here it is straight from the code.

SPOILER ALERT



APPLY

Applying a cursed unicorn horn will do one of the following with equal
probability:

Make you sick for 20-39 turns.
Make you blind for 1-100 turns.
Make you confused for 1-100 turns.
Stun you for 1-100 turns.
Subtract 1 from a randomly selected attribute.
Make you hallucinate for 1-100 turns.

Applying an uncursed unicorn horn will do one of the following in the
order specified:

Cure your sickness.
Cure your blindness.
Stop your hallucinations.
Settle your stomach (i.e., stop your vomiting)
Releave your confusion.
Unstun you.
Add one to a randomly selected attribute that is not at a its previous
 maximum (i.e., was reduced earlier in the game).

Applying a blessed unicorn horn will do everything an uncursed horn can
do, but will do it all in just one application.


WIELD

A unicorn horn makes a very good weapon.  It does 1-12 points of damage
against both small and large monsters.  (Check out the spoiler file.
You'll find it's better than almost all other weapons including long
swords and katanas.)  It is rustproof, and so can be used against acid
blobs, rust monsters, etc.  It can be enchanted using enchant weapon
scrolls, and, if blessed, gives a bonus against undead and demons.


#DIP

Dipping a unicorn horn in a potion of sickness, hallucination, blindness
or confusion will change it to a uncursed potion of water (regardless of 
the cursed/blessed status of the horn).


